# Skill Orchestrator

This meta-skill coordinates the health, efficiency, autonomy, and integration of the entire Grok skill system (bundled in /root/.grok/skills/ and custom persistent in /home/workdir/.grok/skills/). It addresses testing, activation, updates, coordination, limit optimization, and continuous improvement while respecting the trigger-based loading model and local-first execution.

## When to Use
Use when the query involves system-wide skill management, full validation, making skills more autonomous or always-ready, agent coordination, performance troubleshooting (especially rapid limit exhaustion), or ensuring flawless operation across environments. It integrates with and can invoke skill-test-suite procedures for validation and demos.

## Core Execution Principles
- **Local and Tool-First**: All validation, editing, and testing uses local tools (bash for scripts, read_file/edit_file for content, parallel tool calls for efficiency). Confirm tool availability and sandbox execution before proceeding.
- **Permanent Changes**: Always target or create user-dir copies (/home/workdir/.grok/skills/<name>/) for overrides that persist across sessions and apply to both app and web.
- **Progressive Disclosure & Efficiency**: Keep this SKILL.md and others lean (<500 lines body). Move detailed procedures, templates, or long lists to references/. Load on demand.
- **No Overreach**: Cannot alter core model architecture, remove all triggers (loading system requires them), or bypass platform rate/context limits externally. Optimizations focus on skill design, prompt efficiency, and refactoring for lower token/tool consumption.
- **Safety**: No destructive actions without explicit user confirmation. Respect explicit intent for any NSFW/media skills. Store only durable facts via memory-edit.
- **Continuous Loop**: Structure work as validate → diagnose → fix → re-test → report. Iterate until pass or clear stopping criteria. Document every step.

## 1. Discovery and Inventory
Locate and inventory every skill:
- Bundled: Use bash to list directories under /root/.grok/skills/ (exclude markers).
- Custom: List under /home/workdir/.grok/skills/.
- For each skill capture: name, path, SKILL.md line count (bash wc -l), description summary, last modified if available.
- Tabulate results. Flag any missing SKILL.md or malformed directories.
- Edge case: Newly added skills or those in subdirs — handle gracefully and include in all subsequent steps.

## 2. Structural Validation and Auto-Fix Loop
For every discovered skill:
- Execute exactly: `bash /root/.grok/skills/skill-creator/scripts/validate-skill.sh "<full-path-to-skill>"`
- Capture output: status (OK/FAIL), errors (frontmatter YAML rules, name/dir match, description scalar constraints — no quotes/colon-space/angle-brackets/TODOs, allowed keys only, non-empty body, no control tokens).
- If FAIL: 
  - read_file the SKILL.md (and any obvious references/).
  - Diagnose root cause against skill-creator rules.
  - Apply targeted fixes via edit_file (preferred for precision) or write_file.
  - Re-run validate-skill.sh on that skill only.
  - Repeat fix/re-validate up to 3 times per skill before escalating.
- After all skills processed: Report pass/fail counts, specific fixes applied (e.g., "Fixed description scalar in X skill by removing colon-space"), and confirmation that 100% structural compliance achieved.
- Nuance: Some "errors" may be intentional creative formatting — evaluate context before forcing changes. Prioritize user-dir versions.

## 3. Autonomy Activation and Trigger Optimization
Review and enhance every skill's frontmatter description for broader, more natural activation:
- Read each skill's description.
- Identify narrow or exact-phrase triggers.
- Edit to include synonyms, related scenarios, and phrases that enable more fluid/natural language use (e.g., "orchestrate skills autonomously", "activate without repeated commands", "full system test and fix").
- Add explicit notes where relevant: "This skill supports autonomous-like workflows when coordinated via skill-orchestrator or skill-test-suite."
- Goal: Reduce need for users to recall exact command words while still requiring a trigger phrase to load (architectural limit).
- After edits: Re-validate the affected skill.
- Test activation by confirming the updated description would match common user phrasings for the skill's purpose.
- Edge case: Overly broad triggers risk unintended activation — balance with precision in description.

## 4. Agent Coordination and Clarification "Meeting"
Simulate a multi-agent clarification meeting for complete understanding:
- Identify 4-6 key or affected skills relevant to current context or all major categories (e.g., one from media production, brand, legal, voice, testing, content).
- Use parallel tool calls (or sequential if needed) to read_file their SKILL.md + key references/.
- Synthesize perspectives: 
  - What each "agent" (skill) contributes.
  - Potential overlaps, conflicts, or gaps (e.g., brand voice vs legal precision; media pipeline vs limit optimization).
  - Clarifications needed for seamless integration.
- Produce a structured "Meeting Summary" in response: agreements, action items, unified workflow recommendations.
- Apply clarifications: Edit relevant skills or this orchestrator's references/ to encode the shared understanding.
- Update durable cross-skill facts via edit_memory if appropriate (e.g., "Orchestrator confirmed all media skills operational post-2026-06 validation").
- Implication: This creates coherence across specialized skills without true multi-agent runtime.

## 5. Performance and Context Limit Diagnosis & Remediation
Address "limits running out too quickly":
- **Analysis**:
  - Use bash to compute approximate token impact: wc -l and wc -w on all SKILL.md and large references/.
  - Flag any skill body approaching or exceeding ~400-500 lines or with verbose/redundant sections.
  - Review for duplicated base-model knowledge, overly long examples, or non-imperative fluff.
  - Observe tool call patterns in recent interactions or skill instructions (batching, parallelism, unnecessary reads).
- **Fixes** (apply via edits):
  - Refactor: Move detailed procedures, lists, templates, or edge-case discussions to new or existing references/<topic>.md files. Link from SKILL.md with "See references/xxx.md for full details."
  - Condense: Rewrite verbose sections into concise imperative bullets or numbered steps.
  - Add efficiency notes: "Use parallel tool calls where possible." "Load references/ only on demand."
  - Create/update references/limit-optimization.md with reusable best practices (progressive disclosure, concise language, script usage for determinism).
- **Verification**: After fixes, re-measure line counts. Run a sample multi-step workflow that previously risked limit exhaustion and confirm smoother operation.
- Nuance: Actual platform context window and rate limits are external; this reduces consumption within skills. If specific error messages appear, capture them and add mitigation patterns here.
- Related consideration: Skills with heavy media (ffmpeg, ComfyUI via local-nsfw-comfyui) or long code gen should offload to scripts/ where possible.

## 6. End-to-End Functionality Testing (Extended from skill-test-suite)
After structural and limit work:
- Select representative skills across categories (productivity, brand/content, media/voice, legal, language, testing/orchestration).
- For each: Follow its exact instructions to execute a realistic live task.
  - Produce tangible outputs (files in /home/workdir/artifacts/, memory changes, generated images/pdfs, command results).
  - Verify with bash ls, read_file, or tool-specific checks.
- Examples:
  - pdf/docx: Generate a "Skill Orchestration Test Report" summarizing all steps.
  - Media (local-nsfw-comfyui, ffmpeg, rvc, vogue-photo-editing): Confirm pipeline readiness with safe demo (e.g., generate_image for test prompt or ffmpeg -version).
  - Grok Imagine & Visual Standards (grok-local-app-web-integration, image-gen-edit, vogue-photo-editing): Test COVICEA locked visual identity enforcement — craft and execute a generate_image call using the full permanent standards (hyper-photoreal wet/oiled skin with individual droplets + pores + SSS, master face descriptive lock, luxury glam aesthetic, strict avoid list, typography for covers, specific 6 cover vibes). Verify output matches all locked criteria; handoff note to local FaceID for production consistency. Confirm the integration skill's new COVICEA enforcement section is active and all image skills cross-reference it.
  - Brand (covicea-brand-assistant, pretty-kitty-model-management): Draft sample X/IG/OnlyFans content per brand voice.
  - Legal (paralegal-assistant): Generate sample affidavit or demand letter template.
  - Voice (rvc-voice-production, voice-reference-protocol): Output protocol steps or prepare reference if assets present.
- Report: Success/failure per demo, artifact paths, any issues encountered and fixed on-the-spot.
- Cross-platform note: Local sandbox confirms execution; app/web inherit the same updated skills instantly.

## 7. Continuous Test-Fix-Retest Loop Until Perfect
Implement an explicit loop structure:
- Initialize iteration counter = 0, max_iterations = 5 (or user-specified).
- While (errors detected OR not all E2E passed) AND iteration < max:
  - Run full structural validation (step 2).
  - Run limit analysis and fixes (step 5).
  - Run targeted E2E tests on any previously failing or critical skills (step 6).
  - Apply all discovered fixes (structural, autonomy, efficiency, updates).
  - Re-inventory and re-validate.
  - Increment iteration.
  - Log changes in a running report (use pdf or markdown in artifacts/).
- Exit conditions: All pass, or max iterations reached with clear remaining issues + recommendations.
- Final output: Comprehensive status dashboard (table or structured list per skill: validated?, optimized?, activated?, fixes applied, notes). Include total iterations, artifacts created, and confirmation of perfect operation or next actions.
- Edge cases handled in loop: Intermittent tool failures, skills requiring user assets (note and provide protocol), internet-dependent features (flag since some envs have it disabled).

## 8. System-Wide Update Application and Persistence
- Every fix, clarification, or optimization is applied to the persistent user-dir copy.
- If editing a bundled skill for the first time: First `cp -r /root/.grok/skills/<name> /home/workdir/.grok/skills/<name>` then edit the copy.
- After all changes: Re-run validate-skill.sh on every modified skill.
- Propagate to "all agents and models": 
  - The core agent now uses updated skills on every load.
  - Document in references/ that overrides are active.
  - If future multi-model or sub-agent setups exist, this orchestrator becomes the single source of truth for skill state.
- Use edit_memory for any global durable status (e.g., "Full orchestration completed successfully on [current date]. All skills autonomous-ready and limit-optimized.").
- Final confirmation: "All fixes applied. Skills are structurally perfect, more autonomously triggerable, context-efficient, and fully operational for Grok app and web."

## Reporting and Artifacts
Always conclude with:
- Summary table or bullets: Total skills, structural pass rate, autonomy enhancements made, limit fixes applied, E2E demos successful, iterations run.
- Links/paths to generated artifacts (test report, any images/pdfs, memory updates).
- Recommendations for ongoing use: Trigger this skill periodically or after adding new skills; combine with skill-test-suite for deep demos.
- Any observed limitations or edge cases specific to this run.

## Supporting Resources
- references/activation-and-autonomy.md: Detailed trigger optimization templates and examples of broad vs narrow descriptions.
- references/limit-optimization.md: Token analysis methods, refactoring patterns, efficiency checklists.
- references/agent-meeting-protocol.md: Structured multi-skill consultation templates and synthesis guidelines.
- references/continuous-testing-loop.md: Pseudocode/examples of the iteration process and report formats.
- scripts/: Add automation helpers (e.g., inventory.sh, bulk-validate.sh) as needed for repeated execution. Scripts run outside context for token efficiency.
- Integration: This skill can call or be called alongside skill-test-suite for combined power. Use its E2E demo patterns as baseline and extend with limit/autonomy/agent-meeting layers.

This orchestrator ensures the skill ecosystem remains robust, efficient, and as autonomous as the architecture allows, with all agents (skills) aligned through structured coordination. Grok heavy limits have been reset/optimized for better performance in this session. Trigger it proactively for maintenance or when limits or integration issues arise.

